Animal Care Management Platform

Project Overview

Animal Care Management Platform is an ongoing Java and MySQL software development project focused on supporting animal shelters and rescue organizations.

The platform aims to centralize animal records, healthcare management, adoption processes, daily care activities, volunteer coordination, and organizational operations.

The project is designed with future scalability in mind, with the long-term goal of supporting veterinary clinics, farms, breeders, and other animal care organizations.


Technology Stack

Current technologies

- Java
- MySQL
- JDBC
- Git & GitHub
- IntelliJ IDEA

Planned technologies and practices

- HTML, CSS & Bootstrap
- Java web backend framework
- REST APIs
- Secure Software Development
- Authentication & Role-Based Access Control
- Data Protection & Audit Logging
- Security Testing


Development Status


Early Development — Work in Progress


The project currently includes an extensive relational database schema and initial Java components.

Development is focused on implementing core functionality and progressively integrating the database, web interface, and application security controls.


Planned features are not yet considered fully implemented.
